<!--
  tools/clean-install.wsb

  Phase 7's Done-when, as a double-click: a machine with no Rust, no Node, no
  curl and no OpenSSL, installing the real bundle.

  Run release.bat first. <HostFolder> must already exist or the sandbox
  refuses to start, and the path below only exists after a bundle.

  The host folder is mapped READ-ONLY on purpose. Microsoft's own warning:
  "Changes made during a Sandbox session to a mapped folder with
  write-permissions will persist after a Sandbox is disposed." A clean-install
  test has no business writing to the tree it is testing.

  Networking is on because it has to be: tauri.conf.json uses
  webviewInstallMode "downloadBootstrapper", so the installer fetches the
  WebView2 runtime. That is the documented cost of a small installer, and this
  is where it gets tested rather than assumed.

  What to check once inside (2026-09-15):

    1. The NSIS installer's own graphics — header, sidebar, icons. Never seen.
    2. That it installs and the app launches at all.
    3. That a real HTTPS request succeeds. This is the actual Done-when:
       libcurl, rustls and SQLite are inside the exe, and nothing here has
       ever proved that at runtime on a machine that lacks them.
    4. The allowlist gap in spikes/static-link-proof/check-windows.ps1 —
       four DLLs were added to it without being confirmed present. In a
       sandbox cmd window:

         dir C:\Windows\System32\comctl32.dll C:\Windows\System32\dwmapi.dll
         dir C:\Windows\System32\gdi32.dll C:\Windows\System32\shlwapi.dll

       All four present closes it; delete the "NOT yet eyeballed" comment in
       that script.
    5. Re-run the installer over itself to see the downgrade block behave.

  Requires Windows Pro/Enterprise/Education with the "Windows Sandbox"
  optional feature enabled, on Windows 10 build 18342 or later.
-->
<Configuration>
  <MappedFolders>
    <MappedFolder>
      <!-- Relative to this file. If the sandbox will not start, some builds
           want it absolute: C:\...\src-tauri\target\release\bundle\nsis -->
      <HostFolder>..\src-tauri\target\release\bundle\nsis</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\install</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>true</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
  </MappedFolders>

  <Networking>Enable</Networking>

  <LogonCommand>
    <Command>explorer.exe C:\install</Command>
  </LogonCommand>
</Configuration>
